# =====================================================================
# Customer-Ops — Backend environment
#
# There is ONE canonical, fully-documented template:  ../deploy/.env.example
# Copy THAT to your .env (the quickstart does `cp deploy/.env.example deploy/.env`)
# — it documents every runtime var (core, hardening, auth/SSO, tenancy, Brigade
# federation, the knowledge graph, the AI lane, and all six federation seams).
#
# For a backend-only local run, copy it here and keep the CORE block (DATABASE_URL,
# JWT_SECRET, KEYCLOAK_*); everything else is optional and degrade-clean. Tenancy
# is LIVE — DATABASE_URL is the NOBYPASSRLS `customer_ops_app` role; migrations
# run as the owner (ADMIN_DATABASE_URL).
#
# This file is intentionally NOT a second template (keeping two in sync is what
# let them drift). It only carries the TEST-ONLY vars, which the deploy template
# does not.
#
# Never commit a real .env.
# =====================================================================

# ── Test-only (RLS integration tests; NOT read by the running app) ───────────
# Point the RLS tests at the app (NOBYPASSRLS) and owner roles:
# CUSTOMER_OPS_RLS_TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://localhost:5432/customer_ops
# CUSTOMER_OPS_RLS_OWNER_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://localhost:5432/customer_ops
